# World 2's BASE ocean (SPEC 11, "Base ocean animation"): the terrain strip's water, lines 208-255,
# where the islands and ships stand. Ctrl+L, W, 4 starts mission 4 (Reef Run) on the base pad; the
# chopper flies west over the sea between the base island and the next one and hovers there, so the
# camera is still and only the animation moves the strip's water.
wait-serial "AGK t0" 1000
key 0x63
key 0x28
wait 5
key 0x11
wait 5
key 0x04
wait-serial "AGK world 2 loaded" 400
key 0x63
key 0x28
wait 5
key 0x02
wait 30
press fire 2
wait 60
press left 130
wait 100
screenshot a
wait 32
screenshot b
# The strip's water is colour cycled (SPEC 11, "Base ocean animation"): a swell of 64 frames, a counter-wave of 256 and a
# breathing of 512 run through pens 1, 6 and 7, so a water pixel has one colour at a and another 32 frames later at b.
# The old build's strip is still: a pixel never changes (this was shown red on main's build).
# Pixels are in the open water west of the base island's beach (strip rows 4-9); the pens are the same on all profiles.
expect-color a 8 212 0x267
expect-color b 8 212 0x9DE
expect-color a 90 214 0xBEE
expect-color b 90 214 0x489
expect-color a 55 221 0x267
expect-color b 55 221 0x9DE
expect-serial "AGK start world=2 mission=4"
expect-no-serial "ERR|missing"
expect-no-dropped-frames
expect-max-load 85
expect-min-chip-free 96
